WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.000 --> 00:01.660
[Disclaimer: This series is created solely for entertainment purposes.

3
00:01.680 --> 00:03.330
All individuals, behaviors, places, and events depicted are entirely fictional,

4
00:03.350 --> 00:05.000
with no intention to represent or reference any organizations, departments, occupations, or individuals]

5
00:05.160 --> 00:08.240
I don't want you to be in this terrible relationship.

6
00:08.440 --> 00:11.000
You make the person you're with feel seen

7
00:11.200 --> 00:12.740
and acknowledged.

8
00:12.760 --> 00:13.700
That's the reason

9
00:13.720 --> 00:15.720
I want to be your friend.

10
00:16.000 --> 00:17.620
If you still hold each other back,

11
00:17.640 --> 00:19.360
no one is going to be happy.

12
00:22.280 --> 00:25.000
We were never friends, Chris...

13
00:27.520 --> 00:30.080
What's most important about food is taste.

14
00:30.700 --> 00:33.560
But taste is made up of texture,

15
00:34.280 --> 00:34.920
smell,

16
00:35.440 --> 00:36.720
experience,

17
00:37.400 --> 00:38.880
and memory.

18
00:59.400 --> 01:09.320
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

19
01:09.340 --> 01:14.440
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

20
01:14.460 --> 01:18.340
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

21
01:18.560 --> 01:24.560
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

22
01:24.580 --> 01:34.300
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

23
01:34.320 --> 01:39.360
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

24
01:39.380 --> 01:43.660
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

25
01:43.680 --> 01:52.320
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

26
01:52.840 --> 02:01.480
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

27
02:18.480 --> 02:19.280
Chris,

28
02:20.180 --> 02:22.000
cooking with flowers

29
02:22.020 --> 02:23.460
isn't easy.

30
02:24.820 --> 02:25.940
That means it's possible?

31
02:34.760 --> 02:36.660
Doing something and being good at it are two different things.

32
02:37.400 --> 02:38.240
But I think

33
02:38.300 --> 02:39.380
this is good.

34
03:01.160 --> 03:02.280
I'm buying it,

35
03:03.340 --> 03:04.380
both you...

36
03:06.340 --> 03:07.720
and your food.

37
03:17.840 --> 03:18.840
It's so good.

38
03:20.280 --> 03:21.060
Really?

39
03:21.080 --> 03:22.200
Well done.

40
03:39.480 --> 03:40.640
You got it on your face.

41
03:51.360 --> 03:52.480
Let's give it a try.

42
03:54.280 --> 03:55.920
The terms remain the same.

43
03:57.120 --> 03:58.480
You'll work behind the scenes,

44
03:59.320 --> 04:00.720
and you can start the PR plan right away.

45
04:01.620 --> 04:02.280
Mm.

46
04:02.480 --> 04:04.080
Since she's already done this much...

47
04:04.520 --> 04:06.600
Why not at least let her train the chefs?

48
04:07.280 --> 04:08.480
As for the restaurant,

49
04:08.760 --> 04:10.280
I'll take care of Chris.

50
04:11.040 --> 04:12.840
If customers have questions,

51
04:13.380 --> 04:15.360
she can answer them about her inspiration.

52
04:15.460 --> 04:16.760
I'll take care of her.

53
04:17.120 --> 04:19.880
Chris has to work mostly behind the scenes anyway.

54
04:25.160 --> 04:26.600
Are you that happy?

55
04:29.160 --> 04:30.000
Mm.

56
04:30.600 --> 04:33.760
It feels like my abilities are being acknowledged for the first time.

57
04:36.640 --> 04:38.980
Then, I'll come up with more dishes.

58
04:39.000 --> 04:41.100
There should be a lot of dishes when you're promoting something new,

59
04:41.120 --> 04:41.680
right?

60
04:43.500 --> 04:44.360
I'll be back.

61
04:46.160 --> 04:48.600
Did she really have to rush to come up with new dishes?

62
04:50.680 --> 04:51.960
[COME AGAIN, WE'RE CLOSED]

63
04:57.520 --> 04:58.480
[Calling]

64
05:09.960 --> 05:11.200
Who are you calling?

65
05:12.240 --> 05:13.040
A friend...

66
05:13.680 --> 05:15.640
Your friend who helped you come up with the flower dishes?

67
05:16.840 --> 05:18.120
Mm... yes.

68
05:22.200 --> 05:23.440
That's nice.

69
05:23.720 --> 05:25.720
I want to thank them as well

70
05:26.120 --> 05:28.760
for making you want to help me with my work.

71
05:29.720 --> 05:31.000
And for making us...

72
05:31.180 --> 05:33.240
closer...

73
05:41.320 --> 05:43.040
Don't do this, Nadear.

74
05:44.020 --> 05:45.040
That's right.

75
05:45.520 --> 05:47.600
When we dated,

76
05:49.100 --> 05:51.520
you wouldn't even let me kiss you.

77
05:52.700 --> 05:54.680
Why would I expect anything now?

78
05:56.360 --> 05:57.680
What are you expecting?

79
05:59.160 --> 06:00.880
Change, perhaps?

80
06:02.940 --> 06:05.840
I was willing to accept your flower dishes

81
06:08.400 --> 06:09.840
in hopes that

82
06:10.540 --> 06:12.540
you'd let me...

83
06:13.560 --> 06:16.280
back into our relationship.

84
06:18.720 --> 06:19.840
Back, you say?

85
06:30.280 --> 06:32.320
I used to be in here, didn't I?

86
06:42.680 --> 06:44.720
If my brain has an issue,

87
06:45.520 --> 06:47.600
would my feelings change too, Doctor?

88
06:54.460 --> 06:55.480
The brain...

89
06:55.960 --> 06:57.440
controls your emotions, Chris.

90
07:00.160 --> 07:02.920
My brain tells me I love Nadear,

91
07:04.160 --> 07:06.160
but my feelings say otherwise.

92
07:08.140 --> 07:09.720
Who is right for you then?

93
07:14.960 --> 07:16.680
Can I tell you that?

94
07:17.520 --> 07:18.800
It's a matter of medical ethics.

95
07:18.860 --> 07:20.320
A patient's information is confidential.

96
07:23.040 --> 07:26.760
But you don't seem like that good of a person?

97
07:34.180 --> 07:35.560
That's true,

98
07:36.100 --> 07:37.640
but I'm a good friend.

99
07:39.820 --> 07:41.300
A friend's code.

100
07:41.920 --> 07:43.460
I'll keep my friend's secret to myself.

101
07:46.480 --> 07:48.360
I loved Nadear in the past.

102
07:51.260 --> 07:52.880
That means now...

103
07:57.440 --> 07:59.440
If my memories returned,

104
08:00.760 --> 08:01.880
would the Nadear I knew then

105
08:01.900 --> 08:03.900
be the same person she is now?

106
08:07.880 --> 08:09.240
Speaking as a doctor,

107
08:10.440 --> 08:11.660
I'd say...

108
08:11.680 --> 08:13.680
Our brains are complex.

109
08:15.040 --> 08:16.360
And what if you answer as a friend?

110
08:17.920 --> 08:19.840
Our hearts aren't as complex.

111
08:23.560 --> 08:25.360
Chris is in love with someone else, isn't she?

112
08:28.960 --> 08:29.800
I don't think so.

113
08:31.280 --> 08:32.440
You're lying.

114
08:35.840 --> 08:37.480
It might be that friend.

115
08:39.520 --> 08:41.400
The one who taught her to make those flower dishes.

116
08:41.880 --> 08:43.040
And if it's true...

117
08:43.480 --> 08:44.560
what will you do?

118
08:44.720 --> 08:47.320
I should be asking you that.

119
08:48.920 --> 08:50.520
What should I do?

120
08:52.000 --> 08:53.240
You have to let her go.

121
08:53.400 --> 08:56.000
You know I can't do that.

122
08:58.520 --> 08:59.880
What I mean is...

123
09:00.480 --> 09:01.920
you need to give Chris more freedom.

124
09:03.700 --> 09:05.200
Chris needs to be free

125
09:05.520 --> 09:07.080
before she can choose who to love.

126
09:08.260 --> 09:10.360
And what if she doesn't choose me?

127
09:17.360 --> 09:19.160
Well, you have me.

128
09:28.240 --> 09:29.000
Alright...

129
09:30.960 --> 09:32.520
I'll give it a try.

130
09:37.520 --> 09:40.600
You won't let Chris leave me, right?

131
09:55.660 --> 09:57.400
This plant is hardy.

132
09:59.080 --> 10:00.040
It's easy to take care of

133
10:00.840 --> 10:02.140
and can purify the air as well.

134
10:07.320 --> 10:07.960
Alright,

135
10:10.280 --> 10:12.760
I'll help you out.

136
11:01.880 --> 11:03.240
Oh, Chris?

137
11:03.440 --> 11:04.200
Sun.

138
11:06.240 --> 11:07.540
Is everything alright?

139
11:07.560 --> 11:08.840
Why are you here?

140
11:09.760 --> 11:12.080
I couldn't contact you.

141
11:12.100 --> 11:13.360
Are you alright?

142
11:14.040 --> 11:15.240
I'm alright.

143
11:15.460 --> 11:16.520
What about you?

144
11:16.700 --> 11:18.240
You're not okay, are you?

145
11:21.520 --> 11:22.760
I did it.

146
11:27.800 --> 11:29.640
I told you you got this.

147
11:31.360 --> 11:32.560
It's all thanks to you.

148
11:33.960 --> 11:36.120
Does coming here have something to do with me too?

149
11:37.560 --> 11:39.920
I've always thought about you

150
11:40.440 --> 11:42.120
ever since I made those dishes for the customers.

151
11:46.660 --> 11:47.960
What were you thinking of me?

152
11:50.040 --> 11:51.400
I think it's your compliments?

153
11:52.520 --> 11:55.320
You always know what to say to cheer me up.

154
12:28.760 --> 12:30.040
I kissed you,

155
12:31.100 --> 12:33.100
because I don't want to be just friends.

156
12:39.220 --> 12:40.280
What about you?

157
12:47.800 --> 12:50.600
I don't love Nadear when I'm awake.

158
12:51.080 --> 12:52.800
But every time I dream,

159
12:53.240 --> 12:54.640
it's always about her.

160
12:56.140 --> 12:58.140
The affection still lingers.

161
12:59.160 --> 13:00.480
Your heart

162
13:00.760 --> 13:02.640
might be more complex than your brain.

163
13:04.320 --> 13:05.600
But be careful.

164
13:06.320 --> 13:08.560
This won't only hurt you.

165
13:09.720 --> 13:11.320
It'll hurt the others too.

166
13:22.200 --> 13:23.080
So,

167
13:24.320 --> 13:25.880
are we just friends?

168
13:27.200 --> 13:30.080
Sun, you're a friend I never want to hurt.

169
13:31.740 --> 13:33.280
Not even a little bit.

170
14:08.320 --> 14:09.520
Doctor Prung,

171
14:10.350 --> 14:11.720
you came in without saying anything.

172
14:11.960 --> 14:13.970
Well, when my sister does something,

173
14:13.990 --> 14:16.560
she doesn't seem to tell me either.

174
14:20.240 --> 14:21.080
I didn't tell you,

175
14:21.300 --> 14:22.240
but you knew anyway.

176
14:33.160 --> 14:34.960
This is even worse, Jeen.

177
14:43.340 --> 14:44.200
It's not.

178
14:45.960 --> 14:47.480
We still have hope.

179
14:48.360 --> 14:49.200
What hope?

180
14:52.000 --> 14:52.680
Chris...

181
14:53.080 --> 14:54.680
will never love Nadear.

182
14:56.160 --> 14:57.120
Never.

183
14:59.460 --> 15:01.040
That means...

184
15:01.280 --> 15:02.570
Nadear

185
15:02.590 --> 15:03.880
will love you.

186
15:04.120 --> 15:05.280
Do you really think that?

187
15:08.640 --> 15:09.920
It means...

188
15:10.670 --> 15:11.880
this is the first time

189
15:13.820 --> 15:15.820
I'll do the right thing.

190
15:27.400 --> 15:28.400
Aw...

191
15:29.680 --> 15:30.680
That's good.

192
15:37.560 --> 15:39.660
[Third Person Bar - Bistro]

193
15:39.680 --> 15:40.980
It seems like Chris

194
15:41.000 --> 15:42.720
really enjoys working here.

195
15:46.440 --> 15:47.880
Aren't you worried about her being stressed anymore?

196
15:57.000 --> 15:59.440
I'm going to a flower farm. I'll be back in the evening.

197
16:04.040 --> 16:05.200
With who?

198
16:06.520 --> 16:07.320
A friend.

199
16:07.760 --> 16:09.220
Her working here isn't as worrying as

200
16:09.240 --> 16:11.200
going to the flower farm with her friend again.

201
16:13.680 --> 16:14.480
Wow.

202
16:15.440 --> 16:17.200
It seems like Chris

203
16:17.360 --> 16:19.480
has friends other than you.

204
16:21.520 --> 16:22.200
Yes.

205
16:23.180 --> 16:24.300
It's a good thing

206
16:24.320 --> 16:26.480
I have you, Nan.

207
16:28.400 --> 16:30.320
You'll be by my side, right?

208
16:31.480 --> 16:33.040
I have been with you all this time.

209
16:40.960 --> 16:42.960
[Parking spot]

210
17:06.440 --> 17:07.320
Is that your girlfriend?

211
17:07.560 --> 17:08.560
Why don't you answer it?

212
17:11.200 --> 17:13.640
[Nadear]

213
17:18.880 --> 17:19.720
I'll go back soon.

214
17:20.400 --> 17:21.520
I'll see you this evening.

215
17:27.040 --> 17:28.400
You spoke so politely.

216
17:29.480 --> 17:32.280
Not only is your girlfriend lucky,

217
17:33.440 --> 17:35.720
but you're lucky to have her too, huh?

218
17:39.820 --> 17:41.820
I wanted it to be that way too.

219
17:42.680 --> 17:44.360
What is your girlfriend like?

220
17:46.200 --> 17:46.920
Well...

221
17:47.460 --> 17:49.560
She's a woman with long black hair,

222
17:50.440 --> 17:52.000
and she smiles...

223
17:53.280 --> 17:54.840
so much that I call her "Smiley."

224
17:57.740 --> 17:59.160
Smiley...?

225
18:01.600 --> 18:02.400
Smiley.

226
18:10.040 --> 18:12.800
[Third Person]

227
18:15.047 --> 18:17.847
[Third Person]

228
18:19.127 --> 18:20.707
The hotel

229
18:20.727 --> 18:24.087
picked up the edible flowers a couple of hours ago.

230
18:24.347 --> 18:25.727
It was an urgent order.

231
18:25.987 --> 18:27.647
We truly apologize,

232
18:27.807 --> 18:29.887
but we do have other products you can take a look at.

233
18:29.987 --> 18:31.007
It's alright.

234
18:31.027 --> 18:32.767
We came without an appointment.

235
18:35.027 --> 18:37.287
Not even a little bit left...?

236
18:42.887 --> 18:44.327
You have tulips here?

237
18:44.687 --> 18:45.627
Yes.

238
18:45.647 --> 18:47.787
Would you like to see them? I'll tell the employees to guide you there.

239
18:47.807 --> 18:48.527
Yes, please.

240
18:48.887 --> 18:49.907
Thank you.

241
18:56.927 --> 18:57.887
Why are you smiling?

242
18:59.167 --> 19:00.287
Let's take some photos together.

243
19:02.607 --> 19:03.367
Let's go!

244
19:25.327 --> 19:26.367
Let's take a picture.

245
19:27.357 --> 19:27.887
Come on.

246
19:31.287 --> 19:32.007
Here.

247
19:59.027 --> 20:00.447
Chris, why are you looking at me like that?

248
20:00.887 --> 20:02.247
I'm just a bit surprised.

249
20:02.547 --> 20:04.247
I thought you only liked roses.

250
20:08.667 --> 20:11.167
If someone changes what they like,

251
20:12.687 --> 20:14.607
will their feelings stay the same?

252
20:17.767 --> 20:19.167
If I like tulips,

253
20:20.767 --> 20:22.007
not roses,

254
20:23.447 --> 20:25.447
will you still want to be friends with me?

255
20:29.927 --> 20:31.207
I like roses

256
20:32.427 --> 20:33.627
because I like you.

257
20:35.247 --> 20:37.407
But if you choose to like tulips,

258
20:39.527 --> 20:41.487
I'll like them too.

259
20:45.367 --> 20:46.287
Thank you.

260
20:48.487 --> 20:50.047
Keep your promise, alright?

261
21:07.807 --> 21:09.487
This feels familiar, huh?

262
21:12.447 --> 21:14.127
But today isn't the same.

263
21:14.987 --> 21:15.927
Why?

264
21:17.567 --> 21:19.087
Because we're just friends.

265
21:22.707 --> 21:23.447
Mm.

266
21:25.887 --> 21:27.327
Can you tell me why?

267
21:38.747 --> 21:40.367
The reason is...

268
21:41.127 --> 21:43.127
Don't be a bad person because of me, Sun.

269
22:01.127 --> 22:02.767
Do you have someone else?

270
22:13.527 --> 22:14.927
Why do you ask me that?

271
22:15.247 --> 22:16.967
Why aren't you denying it?

272
22:18.767 --> 22:20.487
You do know

273
22:21.087 --> 22:22.647
what our relationship is, don't you?

274
22:22.967 --> 22:24.727
But we're still dating.

275
22:26.607 --> 22:30.087
I won't let anyone come between us.

276
22:35.407 --> 22:36.527
If I do, I'll tell you.

277
22:37.907 --> 22:39.127
If you didn't,

278
22:41.807 --> 22:43.727
then why did you change?

279
22:46.787 --> 22:48.167
I can't even remember

280
22:48.987 --> 22:50.287
who I used to be,

281
22:51.527 --> 22:53.047
so how could I change?

282
22:53.887 --> 22:55.407
But I do...

283
22:57.827 --> 23:00.047
You used to care more about me.

284
23:01.327 --> 23:02.847
You heard me out.

285
23:03.687 --> 23:06.087
You listened to me.

286
23:06.487 --> 23:08.247
You trusted me.

287
23:09.647 --> 23:11.847
You never asked to break up with me.

288
23:13.827 --> 23:16.047
You used to make me smile.

289
23:21.847 --> 23:24.207
I want you to remember.

290
23:44.087 --> 23:44.967
Chris!

291
23:45.327 --> 23:46.367
Chris!

292
23:53.607 --> 23:54.527
Chris...

293
23:57.507 --> 23:59.767
I've always looked at you...

294
24:05.547 --> 24:08.087
I could feel your eyes

295
24:08.567 --> 24:10.687
always watching me.

296
24:11.207 --> 24:12.687
Is someone looking at me?

297
24:14.567 --> 24:15.407
Yeah.

298
24:15.607 --> 24:16.927
She didn't even look away.

299
24:17.687 --> 24:19.807
Ugh, what the heck is wrong with her?

300
24:20.727 --> 24:22.207
She's the new kid

301
24:22.447 --> 24:24.327
we asked to join our group yesterday.

302
24:24.567 --> 24:25.207
Huh?

303
24:25.747 --> 24:26.407
Mm.

304
24:26.887 --> 24:28.227
After talking to her...

305
24:28.247 --> 24:30.007
she seems pretty nice.

306
24:30.107 --> 24:33.067
She started school a month after us because...

307
24:33.607 --> 24:35.527
she moved with her dad after he changed jobs.

308
24:47.147 --> 24:47.727
Ow.

309
24:49.647 --> 24:50.527
Chris!

310
25:00.487 --> 25:01.207
You!

311
25:01.347 --> 25:02.847
Run three laps around the field!

312
25:13.947 --> 25:16.007
Hey! Be more careful.

313
25:16.027 --> 25:18.407
Do you want to get caught buying stuff from outside the school?

314
25:21.807 --> 25:23.007
Hey, you two!

315
25:23.067 --> 25:24.247
What are you doing?!

316
25:24.807 --> 25:25.407
Run!

317
25:27.167 --> 25:28.167
Get up there!

318
25:28.187 --> 25:29.027
Go!

319
25:31.407 --> 25:32.687
Get down, get down.

320
25:42.567 --> 25:44.327
Why did we have to run this far?

321
25:45.747 --> 25:47.247
Well, I was scared.

322
25:52.327 --> 25:53.247
Do you think...

323
25:54.767 --> 25:56.527
he'll find us here?

324
25:58.447 --> 25:59.387
Maybe he will

325
25:59.407 --> 26:01.647
if you keep letting the smell of meatballs waft around like this.

326
26:07.907 --> 26:08.787
Did you know?

327
26:08.807 --> 26:10.807
This is my first time skipping class.

328
26:12.927 --> 26:15.547
If you weren't waiting for your food out in the open like that,

329
26:15.567 --> 26:17.287
you wouldn't have had your first time like this.

330
26:17.847 --> 26:19.447
We had to run for our lives, you see?

331
26:21.207 --> 26:22.407
It was fun, though.

332
26:23.647 --> 26:24.327
Huh?

333
26:26.167 --> 26:27.607
I said,

334
26:27.627 --> 26:29.927
skipping class with you today was fun.

335
26:32.407 --> 26:33.207
Want some?

336
26:43.207 --> 26:44.207
Smiley...

337
26:52.927 --> 26:54.047
It's me...

338
26:56.247 --> 26:58.407
Please be alright...

339
27:12.627 --> 27:14.807
You love the Nadear in your memories,

340
27:15.967 --> 27:17.847
but you want to break up with this Nadear?

341
27:21.087 --> 27:22.007
Why?

342
27:25.947 --> 27:27.487
Nadear used to smile a lot,

343
27:28.327 --> 27:29.687
until she loved me.

344
27:31.167 --> 27:32.247
That's a classic reason

345
27:32.847 --> 27:34.607
for breaking up.

346
27:35.447 --> 27:36.887
Is it really for her?

347
27:39.687 --> 27:42.327
Are you a psychiatrist or an expert at hitting a sore spot?

348
27:43.447 --> 27:45.127
I told you, I'm your friend.

349
27:46.027 --> 27:48.027
I even meet you outside.

350
27:53.527 --> 27:56.047
If I could fall in love with Nadear from the past,

351
27:57.447 --> 27:58.867
but not with

352
27:58.887 --> 28:00.287
the Nadear I know now,

353
28:01.287 --> 28:02.687
shouldn't that mean I should break up with her?

354
28:02.827 --> 28:05.087
Does this have anything to do with the new friend you just met?

355
28:08.847 --> 28:10.767
I never wanted to be just friends with her.

356
28:18.867 --> 28:22.067
[Third Person]

357
28:24.416 --> 28:27.116
[Third Person]

358
28:39.716 --> 28:41.036
You again?

359
28:43.176 --> 28:44.476
Shouldn't I be asking you that?

360
28:45.316 --> 28:47.956
You know full well the reason

361
28:48.096 --> 28:49.036
people come here.

362
28:50.536 --> 28:52.036
I can't contact Sun.

363
28:54.636 --> 28:56.836
I know what Sun thinks of you,

364
28:57.316 --> 29:00.356
but she can't move on from you because you act like this.

365
29:01.336 --> 29:03.756
She already has a lot of problems in her life.

366
29:04.676 --> 29:06.876
Can't you keep your distance from her?

367
29:09.156 --> 29:10.556
Is there something going on?

368
29:18.916 --> 29:19.956
Hello, Sun,

369
29:20.136 --> 29:21.116
where are you?

370
29:21.556 --> 29:22.756
Can we meet?

371
29:24.156 --> 29:25.876
I want to talk about something.

372
29:28.896 --> 29:29.516
Huh?

373
29:31.036 --> 29:32.436
Then can I go with you?

374
29:38.336 --> 29:39.836
Excuse me, I'd like to change my destination.

375
29:41.116 --> 29:42.116
Okay.

376
29:45.156 --> 29:48.676
[VERITY SKIN CLINIC]

377
30:02.836 --> 30:03.596
How are you doing?

378
30:07.776 --> 30:09.036
Is this cocoa?

379
30:19.756 --> 30:20.836
I feel better now.

380
30:21.676 --> 30:22.916
You're so stressed, aren't you?

381
30:25.116 --> 30:25.956
Mm...

382
30:27.146 --> 30:28.876
Looking at the expenses...

383
30:29.536 --> 30:31.156
it's quite troubling to me.

384
30:35.356 --> 30:36.876
I was in an accident,

385
30:38.396 --> 30:40.916
so my father sent me abroad for treatment.

386
30:41.856 --> 30:43.036
Now that I've recovered,

387
30:45.996 --> 30:48.476
I want to repay my debts to my father.

388
30:50.956 --> 30:52.116
But look at this...

389
31:00.136 --> 31:01.396
An accident?

390
31:02.836 --> 31:03.676
When did it happen?

391
31:07.396 --> 31:09.036
Four years ago...

392
31:12.616 --> 31:13.836
That was around the same time as mine.

393
31:14.716 --> 31:15.516
Yeah.

394
31:18.356 --> 31:20.236
There is so much to think about,

395
31:21.436 --> 31:23.356
so everything seems necessary.

396
31:27.436 --> 31:29.436
Actually, I have some savings...

397
31:30.996 --> 31:32.196
Don't, Chris.

398
31:37.896 --> 31:39.716
You've just said that we should be friends.

399
31:41.636 --> 31:43.636
We've just known each other.

400
31:45.176 --> 31:46.516
Don't do this...

401
31:49.436 --> 31:50.456
How about this?

402
31:53.156 --> 31:54.836
Let's do what you've told me before.

403
31:58.336 --> 32:00.476
Choose what fits you perfectly

404
32:01.076 --> 32:02.116
so you feel at ease

405
32:02.796 --> 32:03.876
and not uncomfortable.

406
32:08.676 --> 32:09.736
Then...

407
32:13.796 --> 32:15.396
Can you stay here with me?

408
32:17.296 --> 32:19.156
When I'm with you...

409
32:21.896 --> 32:23.396
I feel exactly like that.

410
32:28.436 --> 32:29.896
[VERITY SKIN CLINIC] ["Reveal The True You"]

411
32:29.916 --> 32:32.236
Is there anything else you'd like to put in this room?

412
32:33.196 --> 32:34.776
I think so.

413
32:34.796 --> 32:36.176
Let me think about it.

414
32:36.196 --> 32:37.556
Don't go over budget, okay?

415
32:41.476 --> 32:44.316
I think this equipment can only be placed here.

416
32:46.636 --> 32:48.596
But we already went way over budget.

417
32:48.836 --> 32:50.836
If we buy this equipment,

418
32:50.976 --> 32:52.796
we won't have enough money for the more important one.

419
32:53.556 --> 32:55.496
If we put both pieces of equipment there,

420
32:55.516 --> 32:57.416
it...it really won't work out.

421
32:57.436 --> 32:59.196
Is there anywhere else we can cut back?

422
32:59.556 --> 33:01.056
I agree with you, Doctor Sun.

423
33:01.076 --> 33:02.436
This is perfect.

424
33:02.576 --> 33:03.876
It's not very risky either.

425
33:05.796 --> 33:07.776
I didn't come up with it.

426
33:07.796 --> 33:08.876
Chris helped me.

427
33:08.936 --> 33:09.956
Wow...

428
33:11.356 --> 33:14.076
Iced lemon tea can help in hot weather like this.

429
33:14.096 --> 33:14.896
- This is yours, Doctor. - Thank you.

430
33:14.916 --> 33:15.656
Thank you.

431
33:15.676 --> 33:16.316
Here.

432
33:16.876 --> 33:17.516
Here.

433
33:18.316 --> 33:19.436
This is yours.

434
33:19.796 --> 33:20.496
Thanks.

435
33:20.516 --> 33:21.276
Are you tired?

436
33:21.496 --> 33:22.396
A little bit.

437
33:26.176 --> 33:27.236
I'm impressed.

438
33:27.556 --> 33:29.156
Ms. Chris, you're quite talented.

439
33:35.056 --> 33:37.116
She's very detail-oriented

440
33:40.156 --> 33:41.876
and caring.

441
33:49.396 --> 33:50.276
That's nice.

442
33:50.516 --> 33:53.516
Then...can we ask you to be our consultant?

443
33:57.236 --> 33:58.276
Of course.

444
33:58.716 --> 33:59.716
Thank you so much.

445
34:02.376 --> 34:03.436
Here, I'll hold it for you.

446
34:04.876 --> 34:06.556
Overall, this looks okay now.

447
34:07.916 --> 34:09.756
I like being useful.

448
34:10.996 --> 34:12.276
But right now...

449
34:12.596 --> 34:14.756
I'm more curious about

450
34:15.516 --> 34:18.076
how Sun acts like she knows me well.

451
34:24.616 --> 34:27.116
Are you thanking me by buying me something you like to eat?

452
34:28.276 --> 34:29.816
Give it a taste.

453
34:29.836 --> 34:31.556
You might like it, Chris.

454
34:39.516 --> 34:40.436
Yes,

455
34:40.796 --> 34:41.996
I do like it...

456
34:43.316 --> 34:44.676
How did she know that?

457
34:45.196 --> 34:46.816
Your face is very telling.

458
34:52.876 --> 34:53.876
You finally smiled.

459
34:54.736 --> 34:55.316
Hm?

460
34:56.716 --> 34:58.956
Well, you hardly smiled today.

461
35:00.516 --> 35:03.156
My life isn't exactly full of things to smile about.

462
35:04.436 --> 35:05.196
So...

463
35:05.576 --> 35:07.156
You came to see me. Is something going on?

464
35:10.156 --> 35:11.876
I came to see your smile.

465
35:12.716 --> 35:13.356
Hm?

466
35:17.596 --> 35:18.396
So...

467
35:19.156 --> 35:20.276
Seen enough?

468
35:35.476 --> 35:38.676
Didn't you say that Chris remembered dating me in high school?

469
35:41.196 --> 35:42.596
Hello, Prung.

470
35:42.836 --> 35:44.556
I'm sorry, I didn't see you there.

471
35:47.876 --> 35:49.036
It's okay, Dear.

472
35:49.596 --> 35:51.996
Prung...already knew everything.

473
35:55.196 --> 35:56.796
Chris remembers that.

474
35:57.156 --> 35:58.556
I already talked to her.

475
36:01.076 --> 36:02.916
Then why isn't she falling for me yet?

476
36:03.936 --> 36:05.236
She's a doctor,

477
36:05.516 --> 36:06.916
not a shaman.

478
36:07.356 --> 36:08.796
She can't make love potions.

479
36:09.776 --> 36:10.396
Prung.

480
36:14.836 --> 36:17.156
It's because you only focus on the past.

481
36:17.396 --> 36:19.676
The "past" that can't be changed,

482
36:20.116 --> 36:21.796
instead of the present.

483
36:22.716 --> 36:24.356
It's not just about her amnesia,

484
36:24.916 --> 36:26.756
but also about a relationship between lovers.

485
36:27.196 --> 36:29.076
A relationship should be about the present.

486
36:35.716 --> 36:37.156
You wouldn't understand

487
36:38.076 --> 36:39.116
how important the "past"

488
36:39.396 --> 36:41.516
is to me.

489
36:51.636 --> 36:53.036
Are you sure you don't want me to drive you home?

490
36:53.296 --> 36:55.456
You already have a lot to think about. Rest up.

491
36:59.576 --> 37:00.436
Thanks.

492
37:04.996 --> 37:05.556
Sun,

493
37:12.816 --> 37:14.596
something sweet to help relieve stress.

494
37:25.476 --> 37:26.636
I'll go now.

495
37:28.236 --> 37:28.956
Mm.

496
37:31.236 --> 37:35.176
♫Your smile is always so bright♫

497
37:35.196 --> 37:39.116
♫The smile imprinted in my heart♫

498
37:40.556 --> 37:46.136
♫Shining like the Sun♫

499
37:46.156 --> 37:48.455
♫Providing warm embrace,♫

500
37:48.480 --> 37:51.802
♫Always being near, hugging you tight,♫

501
37:51.827 --> 37:55.916
♫So you don't shed a tear♫

502
37:56.436 --> 38:01.956
♫If you had to face the storm,♫

503
38:03.916 --> 38:05.076
Thank you...

504
38:06.436 --> 38:10.316
♫The Sun will be there, shining in the sky♫

505
38:11.876 --> 38:14.956
Thank you for not making me regret coming back here.

506
38:20.356 --> 38:23.396
[Third Person]

507
38:25.720 --> 38:28.420
[Third Person]

508
39:12.700 --> 39:15.180
[Happy Anniversary]

509
39:25.560 --> 39:27.500
The accident that happened four years ago

510
39:28.100 --> 39:30.180
almost took you away from me.

511
39:33.580 --> 39:35.320
I called your name every day

512
39:37.040 --> 39:38.460
until you regained consciousness.

513
39:40.100 --> 39:43.460
But you kept staring out the window with tears in your eyes,

514
39:44.260 --> 39:46.580
and refused to talk for five months.

515
39:48.060 --> 39:50.420
You had severe depression.

516
39:51.080 --> 39:52.620
Your body was wounded.

517
39:52.940 --> 39:54.940
You were traumatized.

518
39:55.600 --> 39:57.980
Your brain shut out the pain,

519
39:58.840 --> 40:00.540
blocking out everything else.

520
40:08.580 --> 40:09.540
Jeen.

521
40:15.260 --> 40:17.180
Then you started to remember.

522
40:20.020 --> 40:20.700
Here.

523
40:22.280 --> 40:23.620
Did you buy these to give to people?

524
40:24.780 --> 40:25.660
No,

525
40:25.820 --> 40:27.060
they're offerings for Buddha.

526
40:28.060 --> 40:29.820
Then no thanks. I don't want to take one meant for Buddha.

527
40:30.500 --> 40:32.180
This one isn't an offering.

528
40:32.920 --> 40:34.580
I want to give it to you.

529
41:03.920 --> 41:06.980
You lost your parents in that accident,

530
41:09.480 --> 41:10.600
while I...

531
41:13.460 --> 41:15.100
I lost you.

532
41:19.240 --> 41:20.620
I only thought

533
41:20.980 --> 41:24.500
I wanted you to remember how we used to love each other.

534
41:26.260 --> 41:28.500
I wanted our relationship to go back to how it used to be,

535
41:30.700 --> 41:34.500
and that made me completely ignore what we have now.

536
41:37.480 --> 41:38.700
I'm sorry.

537
41:43.180 --> 41:44.020
Nadear...

538
41:44.820 --> 41:45.740
Chris...

539
41:53.460 --> 41:56.220
I asked you not to break up with me,

540
41:58.700 --> 42:00.500
not because of my parents,

541
42:05.300 --> 42:07.180
but because I love you.

542
42:12.820 --> 42:14.980
Can you give me another chance?

543
42:23.980 --> 42:24.940
I can't, Nadear.

544
42:26.000 --> 42:27.220
I can't love you.

545
42:28.680 --> 42:29.900
Chris, why?

546
42:30.600 --> 42:32.260
You only have me.

547
42:34.680 --> 42:36.860
The one who laughs while looking at you.

548
42:39.580 --> 42:41.660
The one who skipped class with you.

549
42:42.580 --> 42:44.700
The one who bought you roses.

550
42:45.680 --> 42:47.780
It's all me, Chris.

551
42:50.700 --> 42:51.980
That's not it.

552
42:54.400 --> 42:55.860
That's not it, Nadear.

553
42:56.460 --> 42:57.540
Chris...

554
42:59.800 --> 43:01.820
I can't, I can't, I can't...

555
43:01.840 --> 43:04.480
Nadear, this isn't right. I can't, it's...

556
43:05.680 --> 43:06.540
Chris!

557
43:07.660 --> 43:11.140
I don't know why I'm like this.

558
43:13.840 --> 43:17.220
I don't want to keep living like this anymore, Nadear.

559
43:17.400 --> 43:18.300
Chris...

560
43:31.440 --> 43:32.340
Alright,

561
43:37.300 --> 43:38.460
I give up.

562
43:43.080 --> 43:45.580
Can you give me three months?

563
43:50.700 --> 43:53.660
Three months to go back to how it used to be.

564
43:58.580 --> 44:01.380
Then I won't ask anything from you again.

565
44:14.060 --> 44:15.460
Chris, please?

566
44:51.440 --> 44:53.820
[Happy Anniversary]

567
44:59.340 --> 45:00.660
What do you mean, "three months"?

568
45:01.370 --> 45:03.020
You broke up a long time ago,

569
45:03.880 --> 45:06.700
but you plan to date her again for three months?

570
45:07.960 --> 45:10.060
It's my final gambit.

571
45:11.720 --> 45:12.820
What are you going to do?

572
45:17.060 --> 45:18.660
I'll make Chris

573
45:21.100 --> 45:22.400
mine...

574
45:25.380 --> 45:26.980
by any means necessary.

575
45:32.840 --> 45:34.380
So you acted weird

576
45:35.820 --> 45:37.420
because you want to be friends with me

577
45:38.600 --> 45:40.600
so that you can cut ties with your ex.

578
45:42.900 --> 45:43.700
Mm...

579
45:44.580 --> 45:46.020
But I couldn't do it.

580
45:47.640 --> 45:49.920
And I even gave her three months.

581
45:51.840 --> 45:53.140
You gave in because

582
45:53.780 --> 45:55.060
you still love her, don't you?

583
46:02.820 --> 46:05.100
She used to be someone important to me.

584
46:07.860 --> 46:09.580
This sounds like we're having an affair.

585
46:12.200 --> 46:14.740
I really don't want you to be a bad person because of me.

586
46:16.940 --> 46:19.620
We were wrong from that very first kiss, Chris.

587
46:22.300 --> 46:23.820
Will God punish us?

588
46:25.560 --> 46:26.940
This pain

589
46:27.780 --> 46:29.440
is God's punishment.

590
46:31.280 --> 46:33.620
Can I still make things right?

591
46:35.600 --> 46:36.300
Mm.

592
46:37.380 --> 46:38.300
I'll wait.

593
46:40.860 --> 46:42.020
Wait for what?

594
46:43.660 --> 46:46.660
Three months might be long enough for you to love someone else.

595
46:48.240 --> 46:51.340
Or it might be long enough for you to decide we should be just friends.

596
47:04.620 --> 47:05.980
But three months

597
47:06.040 --> 47:08.420
is long enough for you

598
47:09.160 --> 47:11.160
to tell love from indebtedness.

599
47:24.380 --> 47:25.700
I know what love is

600
47:27.880 --> 47:29.420
ever since I first met you.

601
47:35.940 --> 47:45.680
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

602
47:45.700 --> 47:50.800
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

603
47:50.820 --> 47:54.700
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

604
47:54.920 --> 48:00.920
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

605
48:00.940 --> 48:10.660
♫The storm grows heavier, demanding an answer♫

606
48:11.340 --> 48:12.700
I'll make things right

607
48:13.820 --> 48:15.160
after three months.

608
48:15.360 --> 48:16.620
Don't you think

609
48:17.100 --> 48:19.060
she can keep asking for more time?

610
48:19.540 --> 48:21.540
But it's important to me too.

611
48:21.900 --> 48:23.500
It's really you, huh?

612
48:23.930 --> 48:25.930
How was she doing

613
48:26.620 --> 48:28.020
after that accident four years ago?

614
48:28.200 --> 48:29.740
Sun lost her memories back then.

615
48:30.140 --> 48:31.700
I think Sun got her memories back.

616
48:33.420 --> 48:34.420
Sun...

617
48:35.020 --> 48:36.020
is my friend...?

618
48:49.860 --> 48:59.740
♫The rain keeps splashing beneath our cover,♫

619
48:59.760 --> 49:04.860
♫Once it was a special place for two lovers♫

620
49:04.880 --> 49:08.760
♫There was never enough room for the third♫

621
49:09.040 --> 49:14.920
♫Now, the rain soaks our hearts together♫

622
49:14.940 --> 49:24.720
♫The question that's trapped in my heart♫

623
49:24.740 --> 49:29.800
♫Maybe it's time for you to do your part♫

624
49:29.820 --> 49:34.080
♫Choose the one your heart truly desires♫

625
49:34.100 --> 49:42.980
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫

626
49:43.380 --> 49:52.020
♫Before the last raindrop falls, don't make me shed another tear♫
